  "content": "When an Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) language model processes each token, a routing mechanism (typically a lightweight gating network) evaluates the token and selects a small subset of the model's many \"expert\" feed-forward subnetworks to actually compute on for that token. Instead of activating the entire model for every token, only the chosen experts run their computations, and their outputs are combined (usually as a weighted sum of the experts' outputs) to produce the token's representation going forward. This lets the model maintain a very large total parameter count—improving capacity and performance—while keeping the per-token computational cost low,",
